cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FLY-lab: what a fly connectome adds to controlling a body"
message: "If you use these results, please cite this repository."
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: "Recluse"
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Recluse/FLY-lab"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible experiment comparing five action-selection modules on an
  identical NeuroMechFly body and walking controller: a constant command, a
  two-line reactive rule, the Drosophila connectome (FlyWire materialisation
  783) driving descending neurons, a replay control that breaks the feedback
  loop, and five degree-preserving shuffles of the connectome.
